    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1249">

                <pb facs="1002" n="886" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg886"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/575.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Bevan to
                        the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tampico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 8, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With further reference to my despatch
                    number 1263 of February 21, I have the honor to transmit herewith a copy of a
                    decree and its English translation<anchor n="72" xml:id="d1249-f1"/> issued by
                    Governor Luis Caballero on the first day of March, again extending the time for
                    the presentation of manifests of property located in the State of
                    Tamaulipas.</p>
                <p>This decree postpones until the first of May any action that could be taken by
                    the Carrancista officials relative to the expropriation of <pb facs="1003"
                        n="887" xml:id="pg887"/> foreign property, and gives the property owners
                    ample time to make their manifestations.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thomas H. Bevan.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
